   "source": [
    "# HMMModel Example Execution for Project09\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the execution of our final Project09 implementation. In Project08, we defined an object‑oriented HMMModel class that implemented the Viterbi algorithm. However, when we attempted to extend that original class to include the additional algorithms required for Project09, we immediately encountered structural limitations, which we describe—along with how we ultimately resolved them—in Project09’s README.md file.\n",
    "\n",
    "The execution below therefore calls upon the Python script Project09.py, which comprises a completely redefined HMMModule class built to accommodate all four HMM algorithms: Viterbi, Forward, Backward, and Forward–Backward. This execution also calls upon our supporting module containing dict_maker and StrMatrix, which convert the nested probability dictionaries into log‑space matrices used throughout the algorithms. All execution calls and defining parameters take place within this notebook in labeled cells, with associated outputs immediately after each call.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "## Imports and Formatting Helper Functions:\n",
    "The following cell imports all packages and modules needed to call our script and supporting module for execution in this notebook. The first helper function included directly below the imports is used only for formatting the output matrices produced during execution, strictly for visualization purposes in Jupyter Notebooks and in the GitHub repository for this project, HMM_Class_of_Algorithms." The second helper function adds headers to the numpy array matrices for visualization in a Jupyter Notebook.
   ],
   "id": "8fabf795140af7e0"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "593ec761",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-08T08:52:36.441245Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-08T08:52:36.435515Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "# Import packages and modules\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from project09 import HMMModel\n",
    "from dict_maker import StrMatrix\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, HTML\n",
    "from tabulate import tabulate\n",
    "\n",
    "def show_matrix_html(matrix, float_format=\"{:.3e}\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Function to display matrices output from execution of project09.py in an organized, interpretable format.\n",
    "    Parameters:\n",
    "         matrix (np.array): output matrix from each HMMModel method execution\n",
    "         float_format (str, optional): formatting string for floating point output\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    formatted = []\n",
    "    for row in matrix:\n",
    "        new_row = []\n",
    "        for cell in row:\n",
    "            if isinstance(cell, float):\n",
    "                new_row.append(float_format.format(cell))\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                new_row.append(str(cell))\n",
    "        formatted.append(new_row)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return HTML(tabulate(formatted, tablefmt=\"html\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def add_headers(matrix, states, observation):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Add state labels and observation characters as headers for a DP matrix. This is for\n",
    "    forward and backward algorithms to display headers and hidden states because they are\n",
    "    numpy arrays.\n",
    "    Steps:\n",
    "         Create a header row containing a blank cell followed by each observed character.\n",
    "        Create one row per hidden state, placing the state label in column 0.\n",
    "        Append the corresponding matrix row values after the state label.\n",
    "        Return the combined header row and state-labeled rows as a nested list.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    header_row = [\" \"] + list(observation)\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for i, state in enumerate(states):\n",
    "        rows.append([state] + list(matrix[i]))\n",
    "    return [header_row] + rows\n"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": 61
  },
  {
